    "html": "<p>A straight conductor of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> carries a current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> at right angles to a uniform magnetic field of flux density <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span>. The magnetic force on the conductor is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>. The conductor is replaced by a second conductor of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3L\"></span> carrying a current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2I\"></span>. This second conductor is placed in the same magnetic field at an angle of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30^\\circ\"></span> to the field lines. What is the magnetic force on the second conductor?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.5F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.2F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0F\"></span></p></li></ol>"
